{"v":2,"s":"p","w":3,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Describing motion","b":"<p>Motion is always relative to a <b>reference body</b> (referentno telo). The line an object follows is its <b>path</b> (putanja); the length travelled is the <b>distance</b> s (pređeni put).</p><p>In <b>uniform rectilinear motion</b> (ravnomerno pravolinijsko kretanje), the speed v is constant:</p><div class=\"fx\">s = v · t</div><div class=\"callout\">Cruise control on the highway: the same distance every second.</div>"},{"t":"read","h":"Average speed","b":"<p>Average speed = <b>total distance / total time</b>. It is not the average of the speeds!</p><p>60 km at 30 km/h (2 h) and then 60 km at 60 km/h (1 h): 120 km / 3 h = <b>40 km/h</b>, not 45.</p>"},{"t":"read","h":"Graphs","b":"<ul><li><b>s–t graph</b>: a straight line; the steeper it is, the greater the speed (the slope is v).</li><li><b>v–t graph</b>: a horizontal line; the <b>area under it</b> is the distance.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 134\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Uniform motion. Left: on an s–t graph a steeper line means a faster body. Right: on a v–t graph the area under the line is the distance.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"120\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"20\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"146\" y=\"134\" >t</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">s</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"30\" class=\"kc\" /><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"90\" class=\"k\" /><text x=\"116\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"10\" class=\"acc\">fast</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"10\">slow</text><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"120\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"20\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"306\" y=\"134\" >t</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">v</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"60\" width=\"90\" height=\"60\" rx=\"0\" class=\"a2\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"60\" class=\"kc\" /><text x=\"235\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">area = s</text></svg><figcaption>Uniform motion. Left: on an s–t graph a steeper line means a faster body. Right: on a v–t graph the area under the line is the distance.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"ex","q":"How far does a car go at 72 km/h in 15 minutes?","s":["72 km/h = 20 m/s, 15 min = 900 s.","s = v·t = 20 · 900 = 18 000 m.","Or directly: 72 km/h · 0.25 h = 18 km."],"a":"18 km"},{"t":"num","q":"A runner covers 100 m in 8 s. Speed?","a":12.5,"u":"m/s","e":"100 / 8.","tol":0.01},{"t":"num","q":"10 km in 0.5 h, then 30 km in 0.5 h. Average speed?","a":40,"u":"km/h","e":"40 km / 1 h."},{"t":"mc","q":"On a v–t graph, the distance travelled is:","o":["the slope","the area under the line","the height of the line","the time"],"a":1,"e":"Area = v · t = s."},{"t":"mc","q":"Two lines on an s–t graph — which body is faster?","o":["the one with the steeper line","the one with the flatter line","they’re equal"],"a":0,"e":"Steeper slope = more distance per second."},{"t":"num","q":"At 5 m/s, how long does 1 km take?","a":200,"u":"s","e":"1000 / 5."}]}